{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap","id":852858,"title":"Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines [AP]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-25T01:35:49-07:00","id":852858,"title":"Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines [AP]","content":"<b>EDIT FROM THE YEAR 2021: Google screwed up all the links but they should(?) be fixed now!<br /> <br /> TL;DR: An actual play of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade \u2013 Bloodlines</i> as a Requiem Chronicle. Complete as of 08/05/2018. Thanks for reading!</b> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Bright Lights, Dead City</b></span><br /> <br /> <i>Hello, L.A. You\u2019re up way past your bedtime, aren\u2019t you?</i><br /> <br /> You know this story. Right?<br /> <br /> Boy meets...<br /> <br /> Yeah, you know it. Boy meets girl, girl kills boy, boy rises from the bitter grave-dirt wanting more than just girls. It\u2019s never as simple as that, though, is it? Spilt blood is messy. Gets mixed.<br /> <br /> Gets thin.<br /> <br /> <b>Welcome to L.A.</b><br /> <br /> The nights in Los Angeles are as thin as they come. The Blood runs thin and it\u2019s only getting thinner. Too much lost down the gutter, and all over who got to be shit-king of the psychopaths. Brother against brother, clan against clan. All that good stuff. Ten years past and it still feels like the city\u2019s gonna boil over. Any minute now\u2026<br /> <br /> The Revolution is biding its time. It\u2019s a temporary setback. Opportunity in adversity. Another brick in the wall. The half-hearted <b>Carthian </b>mantras ring out in the bars they pretend to down whiskey in. One day the Ivory Tower will extend itself just a foot too far, and <i>then</i> the Carthians will show them all why they\u2019re called Firebrands. Then it\u2019ll be the bad old days, when every Kindred was her own master, and L.A. bowed to no self-titled monarch with a ten dollar name.<br /> <br /> But not now. Never now.<br /> <br /> The <b>Invictus</b> claim all of which their tentacles can suck life from. They can certainly afford it. The cops, the gangs...even the garbage men. So sure, they \u201cwon\u201d, if you can call that victory. The Carthians got to keep most of their stupid pseudo-Soviet enclaves, and every Lick with a lick of sense knows the Ventrue\u2019s little compromise candidate is a stepping stone for bigger fish. To know <b>Sebastian LaCroix</b> is to hate him, and that\u2019s a kind way of putting it.<br /> <br /> The <b>Sanctified </b>didn\u2019t weather it. All that blood swept them away. The only thing left is a family of corpse fuckers on the edge of town, praying over their departed brethren and communing with the dead as if they aren\u2019t the same damn thing.<br /> <br /> The <b>Ordo Dracul </b>are very content indeed. Blood spilled is blood to analyze. Blood to taste. Let the Invictus and Carthians play politics and miss all the forests for all the trees. The Ordo know it\u2019s on fire.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t speak of the <b>Mother\u2019s Army</b>. Kill them when you find them. <i>Don\u2019t let them take you alive</i>.<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s <b>Chinatown</b>. Even the Shadows can\u2019t see the threads. Someone\u2019s cutting them. Someone\u2019s pulling them out.<br /> <br /> <b>The Usual Suspects</b><br /> <br /> <b>Zach </b>likes to break things. On the ice he\u2019d break noses, and he notched his stick for every fool who checked him, like some boys whittle bedposts. Back in Winnipeg that was enough, but it\u2019s not in L.A., and it\u2019s certainly not for the Kindred. Now, he breaks legs for the Dragons. In exchange they\u2019ve promised to show him how to channel that aggression into something so much grander.<br /> <br /> Alastair has a name only a Serpent could love. Once upon a time, <b>Al</b>'s family did what it had to. He didn\u2019t like that, so he ran. He didn\u2019t run far enough, of course. He never could. He was too good at collecting dirt and spreading it, and becoming a vampire was the natural next step. The Firebrands aren\u2019t good at subtlety, and that\u2019s why they need him. Some say he\u2019s got the luck of the Devil himself.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Obligatory Explanation</b></span><br /> <br /> Welcome to my first AP! I\u2019m co-STing this with a good buddy,<b> Trotsky's Ghost</b>, who will pop up occasionally to troll us.<br /> <br /> Some of you know this plot pretty well. Some of you don\u2019t.<br /> <br /> <b>For those of you who haven\u2019t played <i>Bloodlines</i>: </b>Huge spoilers ahead!<br /> <br /> <b>For those of you who have: </b>Don\u2019t take anything for granted. If you have questions about things that relate back to <i>VTMB</i>, private message me, or use the Spoiler Tags, if you want it to be public.<br /> <br /> This game will be very roughly every other week, Friday or Saturday. I try to have a write-up for my players before game day, so that will roughly correspond with my updates.<br /> <br /> For now, I\u2019m leaving some things about the setting ambiguous. There will be hints as we go along (as well as explicit truths), but we don\u2019t want to give too much away, and we\u2019d rather readers experience the reveals along with the players.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Story So Far...</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 1, &quot;An opening&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <b>Part 1: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35VThBQXZCRGwyN0U/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-zSrQxVCb9wM4UcZqFRFWvw\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...9wM4UcZqFRFWvw</a><br /> <b>Part 2: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35NUtPTzVqTVJ3NTQ/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-LAnvWjkhHlZjhVzWhUXLmg\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...HlZjhVzWhUXLmg</a><br /> <b>Part 3: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35TWdyYjVXbWJCb0E/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-qo9q8QWRGtvBBor56YbRtA\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...GtvBBor56YbRtA</a><br /> <b>Part 4: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35RV9sLW9MbXdreDQ/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-zYwXczqs6ymutAs_pRQXLQ\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...6ymutAs_pRQXLQ</a><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 2, &quot;The first move&quot;<br /> <br /> Part 1: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35WmEzS3BVdHZYa3c/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-pxkyksynr_JijENei8UlAA\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...r_JijENei8UlAA</a><br /> <b>Part 2: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35ZHp0akFJX2tjWUE/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-na4dSdUpd-KabZc1VFWzTg\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...d-KabZc1VFWzTg</a><br /> <b>Part 3:</b> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35dXAxTElkdUdDdkU/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-CCkwdnbckdVEYPW1Tg0HiQ\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...kdVEYPW1Tg0HiQ</a><br /> <b>Part 4:</b> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35WksyVldsVS1ZQUU/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-1CJE66ftsBvSSDNpNoq6Ew\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...sBvSSDNpNoq6Ew</a><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 3, &quot;A sacrifice&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <b>Part 1: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35SERfcm1tTE1EV1k/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-JIpzSqE6zA0caTXPR3iYzw\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...zA0caTXPR3iYzw</a><br /> <b>Part 2: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35OTc0ZEt6bGEyaGc/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-TCORSEf5GMluzIOUjuqGdA\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...GMluzIOUjuqGdA</a><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 4, &quot;A gambit&quot;<br /> <br /> Part 1: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35dTFWUUZJS3RLSG8/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-HSpS7LoCUOw5H-2fXoVbFw\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...UOw5H-2fXoVbFw</a><br /> <b>Part 2: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35SGY1b3lueDc0RVk/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-xUyCr5jKIKLTP-gRhW7unw\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...IKLTP-gRhW7unw</a><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 5, &quot;The queen&quot;<br /> <br /> Part 1: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35U3RVa0w4SE9Ncjg/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-z-MLdUZl_5uflGCxBgUM9Q\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E..._5uflGCxBgUM9Q</a><br /> <b>Part 2: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35VlRGTTNrWklDNms/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-PcR8wIrGUjAn9vllqbkmCQ\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...UjAn9vllqbkmCQ</a><br /> <b>Part 3: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35OVZLWlFuQVdZZEU/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-im501ONAqWBE3MnzR6_4Ug\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...qWBE3MnzR6_4Ug</a><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 6, &quot;The campaign&quot;<br /> <br /> Part 1: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35aXZnVGdIZk1kUEk/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-7oNJ0s1Xr5crqjNxst6Z7w\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...r5crqjNxst6Z7w</a><br /> <b>Part 2: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35UmpKSDNtdGp5b1U/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-KZ4Bc6-FwxTaFvzqQv2xMw\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...wxTaFvzqQv2xMw</a><br /> <b>Part 3: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1M1M_VK85FNmo0RiJ1z7PJoKIk49AE-Tv/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1M1M...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 7, &quot;The endgame&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <b>Part 1: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NXxMgKjcsLKnj7mQ_drUo3PARCDa8t3o/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1NXx...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <b>Part 2: </b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gICA_lJkNU-TxglPudeNfECDcqvad8M6/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gIC...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> <b>Finale: <a href=\"http://the-breakup.libsyn.com/bloodlines-dont-open-it\" target=\"_blank\">Don't Open It</a></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Biographies: From A to Zed</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Al (<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35T2l5YVIzTEs1Zlk/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-8BBEEN2q2hPMW5-XI-9K3A\" target=\"_blank\">Character Sheet</a>)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Name:</b> Alastair Ardent<br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Al<br /> <b>Clan:</b> Daeva<br /> <b>Bloodline: </b>Zelani<br /> <b>Covenant:</b> Carthians<br /> <b>DOB:</b> March 10, 1984<br /> <b>DOD:</b> June 8, 2006<br /> <br /> Al grew up in Chicago, the youngest of five brothers. They were all named after strange or stuffy relations on his Mom\u2019s side of the family. It meant a lot of teasing, a lot of sticking with his other brothers and not branching out much. Even then he liked being alone better, but safety in numbers were how they lived. His mom died when he was ten of a heart attack and his dad was unfit to take care of them, so his eldest brother Atticus took them all in. He didn\u2019t understand until he was sixteen how Atticus took care of them. Work was mentioned, but never elaborated on.<br /> <br /> Eventually he found out they were into broken legs and broken heads, and maybe worse things. He watched. Mac first, and then Stacy started to \u201cwork\u201d too. He figured he\u2019d be expected to as well, then if not later, so he stole some money and got on a bus out to L.A. He\u2019s been there ever since. He figures Atti hates the heat and won\u2019t look for him there.<br /> <br /> Despite running from a criminal family, crime is where he ended up, a fact that used to shame him. He had little money and needed protection, so he joined a gang. Without any brawn to offer, he became their messenger. Turned out he\u2019s good at listening around, hearing things, spying. He even found out there\u2019s people that pay for that sort of information. When he gained enough leverage to leave the gang, he set up shop as an information broker. Not just for crime, but for anything: gossip, celebrities, politicians\u2026the list is long and slimy.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s a useful person to have in your corner, and that\u2019s probably why his sire chose him. The Carthians needed a good information gatherer. But the Firebrands are just his brothers all over again. Al wants to avoid being part of something, but he always manages to be drawn into it thinking that it\u2019ll help awaken some spiritual fire. It never does.<br /> <br /> <b>Touchstone: </b>The owner of the corner store near his house. He was the first person that showed him kindness in L.A., letting him buy cigarettes even though it was clear he couldn\u2019t have been legal. Every week he buys cigarettes there, even though he rarely smokes them anymore.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Zach (<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35eGI3cENkUHNBejA/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-Hcny2251uHJVwI4XVt3GVg\" target=\"_blank\">Character Sheet</a>)</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Name: </b>Zachary Kovalenko<br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Zach, Zach Attack<br /> <b>Clan:</b> Ventrue<br /> <b>Bloodline: </b>R\u00f6tgrafen<br /> <b>Covenant: </b>Ordo Dracul<br /> <b>DOB:</b> August 27, 1985<br /> <b>DOD:</b> January 11, 2006<br /> <br /> Zach was born in Dauphin, Manitoba. Though he never doubted his parents loved him, home was not a comfortable place, especially around report card time. He preferred the rink, where he could out-skate and out-shoot any competitor. Recruited directly out of high school to the minor leagues, he was snatched up by a sharp-eyed recruiter and went to L.A. to play as backup for the Kings. Unfortunately, he fell under the same influences as many young athletes \u2014 cocaine and shady dealings being his particular vices. At one party, he met someone in his mind he can still only call the <b>Whisper</b>\u2026<br /> <br /> He now generally tries to earn a quiet living as after-dark muscle. People wash out all the time in L.A. \u2014 even if he were spotted, who would care? Just another meathead hockey player who couldn't hack it in the NHL.<br /> <br /> Not being very political, the Dragons seemed like a good choice in the All Night Society. The Ordo Dracul need more muscle these nights, and Zach, while not exactly book smart, is a deeper thinker than most give him credit. The Mysteries and the Coils still evade him, but the Sworn of the Axe has shown him plenty about the intersection between brain and muscle.<br /> <br /> <b>Touchstone: </b>Katrina took Alex back to Winnipeg when things hit the wall. Alex is eleven now, and everything Zach wasn't at her age \u2014 small, shy, bookish, and adored, not least by her father. They Skype every week.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>A Ghoulish Conversation</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Zach vs. Romero:</b> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E3WNZf5G35b0JVWXQtQlpuakU/view?usp=sharing&amp;resourcekey=0-1wfcgcZ2oUlm7pL9LBxCjA\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_E...oUlm7pL9LBxCjA</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>Me, as Romero<br /> [REDACTED], as Zach</b></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer