 disliked the prince? Seeing how the meetings with Strauss and Nines act as good opportunities for joining the Carthains and Ordo, maybe having a meeting with a more likeable invictus (Gary after the sewers, maybe?) would do the trick? Also, if they they were newbies, how would you have adapted the tutorial mission from the game to act as an intro to VtR? I'm thinking I might run something like this for my group of friends someday (none of them who have played the game have played the first parts of past Santa Monica and none have played VtR, so newbies works for us).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:23:50-07:00","id":974770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=974754#post974754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to know what happens next, This gangrel will frenzy if more weeks go by without an update.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then have no fear! We're going to be back next week. This delay lasted a lot longer than I intended, and I haven't had the time to work on the summary due to some work related writing, but we will be back, absolutely, on October 1!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=974754#post974754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since you said that this play through could have worked just as well with newbie players/ newly embraced characters, what would you have done differently in that case? In particular, how would you have given the newbies the chance to join the invictus, even if they disliked the prince? Seeing how the meetings with Strauss and Nines act as good opportunities for joining the Carthains and Ordo, maybe having a meeting with a more likeable invictus (Gary after the sewers, maybe?) would do the trick? Also, if they they were newbies, how would you have adapted the tutorial mission from the game to act as an intro to VtR? I'm thinking I might run something like this for my group of friends someday (none of them who have played the game have played the first parts of past Santa Monica and none have played VtR, so newbies works for us).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think for Covenants, we would've let things fall where they may. Off the top of my head, I might've had them interact with a proxy for LaCroix at first, rather than the man himself, and give them a slightly less biased version of the First Estate...probably would've been Mercurio, come to think of it. Maybe promote him to a vampire, rather than a ghoul. On the other hand, I might have just left things as they are, and let them make their own minds up about the Invictus/Carthians. I actually think the tricky thing would've been making the Lancea et Sanctum a viable choice, since they have the least clear analogue in the video game.<br /> <br /> We'd probably use a reeeeeally loose version of the opening tutorial; nothing fancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 09-22-2016, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T11:47:28-07:00","id":975147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=974754#post974754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to know what happens next, This gangrel will frenzy if more weeks go by without an update.<br /> <br /> Also, since you said that this play through could have worked just as well with newbie players/ newly embraced characters, what would you have done differently in that case? In particular, how would you have given the newbies the chance to join the invictus, even if they disliked the prince? Seeing how the meetings with Strauss and Nines act as good opportunities for joining the Carthains and Ordo, maybe having a meeting with a more likeable invictus (Gary after the sewers, maybe?) would do the trick? Also, if they they were newbies, how would you have adapted the tutorial mission from the game to act as an intro to VtR? I'm thinking I might run something like this for my group of friends someday (none of them who have played the game have played the first parts of past Santa Monica and none have played VtR, so newbies works for us).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Personally, I always thought that the idea of a brand new vampire emerging onto the scene and kicking the crap out of all the things you face in Bloodlines to be highly improbable. If you can do that without any training from your sire, then why the hell are the elders in charge of everything? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> From the sounds of it, the players are somewhat more experienced (and better trained) vampires than we were in Bloodlines, which makes the hack and slash approach more of a viable option.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> That being said, I'm interested in seeing the Minx Xiao battle. It's like a knife fight in a cupboard, except your opponent has multiple knives and the cupboard is already cramped enough!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-23-2016, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T12:05:25-07:00","id":975154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=975147#post975147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I always thought that the idea of a brand new vampire emerging onto the scene and kicking the crap out of all the things you face in Bloodlines to be highly improbable. If you can do that without any training from your sire, then why the hell are the elders in charge of everything? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> From the sounds of it, the players are somewhat more experienced (and better trained) vampires than we were in Bloodlines, which makes the hack and slash approach more of a viable option.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.pa