:"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><i><b>Yay, new episode!</b></i></u></span> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:18:31-07:00","id":980096,"title":"","content":"Every time I read these little synopses, I'm overcome with the urge to fire up Bloodlines and play again. I'm not complaining, mind you, but it does make getting *other* things done more difficult.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn a side note, does anyone else think that someone should write the &quot;Bloodlines Chronicle&quot; and give Requiem 2nd Edition it's first story module? And by someone, I mean Yossarian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T22:48:50-07:00","id":980114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=980096#post980096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every time I read these little synopses, I'm overcome with the urge to fire up Bloodlines and play again. I'm not complaining, mind you, but it does make getting *other* things done more difficult.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn a side note, does anyone else think that someone should write the &quot;Bloodlines Chronicle&quot; and give Requiem 2nd Edition it's first story module? And by someone, I mean Yossarian.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sadly, the synopses, while being a fun read, don't pack the same immersion that reading the actual play sessions would in terms of story.<br /> <br /> But yeah, a Bloodlines Requiem conversion would be highly wanted.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although I'm wondering something:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> If the Sabbat are the Circle of the Crone. Then what the hell are the Kuei Jin supposed to be?</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T23:13:48-07:00","id":980124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=980114#post980114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sadly, the synopses, while being a fun read, don't pack the same immersion that reading the actual play sessions would in terms of story.<br /> <br /> But yeah, a Bloodlines Requiem conversion would be highly wanted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of a mind to write up one of my own for y'all after we finish the chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=980114#post980114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I'm wondering something:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> If the Sabbat are the Circle of the Crone. Then what the hell are the Kuei Jin supposed to be?</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a big spoiler, but I'll tag it just the same:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">They're mostly a cult of Jiang-Shi, but that's not the whole story.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T13:00:42-07:00","id":984564,"title":"","content":"I just want to say I'm glad you are sharing your Chronicle with everyone. I've been looking at it since you started it, and have enjoyed how it has all unfolded.<br /> <br /> It amuses me, because it happened at the same time as me trying to make VTMB into a desktop game, which is still in development. I'll admit that some of the changes you've made will likely be put into what I'm doing!<br /> <br /> Just as a small point, you might want to install the game with the latest Unofficial Patch. Wesp5 and others have now taken it to the next level, where they are restoring and finishing off elements - and even quests - that never got finished. the UP read-me contains information about it all, including some things that won't be completed, because they are too incomplete, or other reasons. One thing that was dropped was another area hub - East LA. It was meant to be a Latino/Hispanic-centric hub, from what can be gathered.<br /> <br /> Also, you might be interested to know that there is also an effort to create a prequel to the game, which has new maps in it as well. Just mentioning it, in case you see something that might be of use.<br /> <br /> This is excellent stuff - keep it up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:30:56-07:00","id":984599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=984564#post984564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to say I'm glad you are sharing your Chronicle with everyone. I've been looking at it since you started it, and have enjoyed how it has all unfolded.<br /> <br /> It amuses me, because it happened at the same time as me trying to make VTMB into a desktop game, which is still in development. I'll admit that some of the changes you've made will likely be put into what I'm doing!<br /> <br /> Just as a small point, you might want to install the game with the latest Unofficial Patch. Wesp5 and others have now taken it to the next level, where they are restoring and finishing off elements - and even quests - that never got finished. the UP read-me contains information about it all, including some things that won't be completed, because they are too incomplete, or other reasons. One thing that was dropped was another area hub - East LA. It was meant to be a Latino/Hispanic-centric hub, from what can be gathered.<br /> <br /> Also, you might be interested to know that there is also an effort to create a prequel to the game, which has new maps in it as well. Just mentioning it, in case you see something that might be of use.<br /> <br /> This is excellent stuff - keep it up!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Antitribu mod is also a good one to check out, as it adds a bunch of content, including the Companion mod and a Sabbat ending.<br /> <br /> They also added a bunch of different NPC models, so you don't have clones walking down the streets, and enemy vamps will actually use disciplines against you. Their Samedi model also looks noticeably more disturbing than the Final Nights version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T16:08:09-07:00","id":984640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=984599#post984599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Antitribu mod is also a good one to check out, as it adds a bunch of content, including the Companion mod and a Sabbat ending.<br /> <br /> They also added a bunch of different NPC models, so you don't have clones walking down the streets, and enemy vamps will actually use disciplines against you. Their Samedi model also looks noticeably more disturbing than the Final Nights version.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the tips. Much appreciated.<br /> <br /> Just so you know, I'm already aware of the Antitribu Mod, and TFN. I've tried to watch playthroughs of Antitribu, and they have some interesting ideas, from what I can see. However, I'm not fully sold on it.<br /> <br /> What is likely to now happen is that VTMB is going to be the original painting myself and a friend will be copying onto a new canvas. What I mean is that the city won't be LA, but a fictional city on the coast of California (at present!). It will be using the game hubs as the start point for the geography, then added on to. When you start looking at the hubs, they make sense as a game, but not as a real life city. So, there needs to be reworkings, and alterations. Also, if you have the Plus Patch, you gain more map areas, because some places - like the museum - have additional areas added on, because of content restoration.<br /> <br /> What is amazing, however, is the fact that you can back engineer a ruleset for this game, based on what Troika has given out. Read the text files included in the game, and they tell you things like how combat is calculated. Add to that the Character Sheet, and some other elements, and you have something you can work with. Moreover, the basic test rules play things a little differently. Quite fascinating to see in action.<br /> <br /> What Troika created is a majestic - if flawed - masterpiece, and is what got me interested in the World of Darkness in the first place. A shame they went under...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T19:17:38-07:00","id":984714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=984640#post984640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What Troika created is a majestic - if flawed - masterpiece, and is what got me interested in the World of Darkness in the first place. A shame they went under...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Flawed or not, I played through it from start to finish <i>at least 10 times</i> before I even started looking for mods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T20:36:19-07:00","id":984733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=984564#post984564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to say I'm glad you are sharing your Chronicle with everyone. I've been looking at it since you started it, and have enjoyed how it has all unfolded.<br /> <br /> It amuses me, because it happened at the same time as me trying to make VTMB into a desktop game, which is still in development. I'll admit that some of the changes you've made will likely be put into what I'm doing!<br /> <br /> Just as a small point, you might want to install the game with the latest Unofficial Patch. Wesp5 and others have now taken it to the next level, where they are restoring and finishing off elements - and even quests - that never got finished. the UP read-me contains information about it all, including some things that won't be completed, because they are too incomplete, or other reasons. One thing that was dropped was another area hub - East LA. It was meant to be a Latino/Hispanic-centric hub, from what can be gathered.<br /> <br /> Also, you might be interested to know that there is also an effort to create a prequel to the game, which has new maps in it as well. Just mentioning it, in case you see something that might be of use.<br /> <br /> This is excellent stuff - keep it up!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much for the kind words!<br /> <br /> I keep up with VTMB updates from time to time. I actually still need to do a Nosferatu run through...!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T21:48:13-07:00","id":984748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=984733#post984733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you very much for the kind words!<br /> <br /> I keep up with VTMB updates from time to time. I actually still need to do a Nosferatu run through...!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sadly, it seems they didn't get to finish programming the Nosferatu's clan flaw very well. I found that as long as I don't stand around in one spot for too long, most humans on the surface just ignore me. But on the upside, you get 3 times as much blood from rats than any other clan!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:31:26-07:00","id":985545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=853311#post853311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In fact, if anyone has any mid-2000s goth rock suggestions for our soundtrack, let fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was re-reading the thread, and I had a thought: what about Abney Park, and Aura Noctis? Those two might provide something of use, particularly &quot;The Wrong Side&quot; by Abney Park. Also, have you thought of using &quot;Liquify&quot; by Chiasm?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:47:32-07:00","id":985558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trotsky's Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=879751#post879751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a random internet stranger and not the co-GM, I also have to wonder at just what could possibly be happening to the Voermans. Yossarian seems to have a few hints but through the mystic power of tea leaves, my crystal ball, and haruspexy, I've come up with my own answer for what is so special about the Voremans:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Something very spooky. </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, the Voermans are very interesting characters. Of course, if you pay attention, you realise that Therese is the older sibling, having been born first. Therese is the one who made sure that Jeanette wasn't harmed when they were in the medical facility, engineering their escape. She was the one to persuade Jeanette they needed to be embraced, otherwise they would, eventually, be separated, by death if nothing else. They remind me a little of a pair of twins i used to know; they hated each other, and were always fighting and all sorts. But they couldn't bear to just break the connection to each other. It's a little like that with the sisters in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=912537#post912537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't let this end before they finish &quot;the game.&quot; I would be heartbroken.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter if they finish the game or not. It only matters if they bought it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:17:52-07:00","id":985592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicSwordsman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=922611#post922611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm so excited to see that this is continuing! I really like finding out all the little changes you made to keep it in line with Requiem's setting (like Pisha no longer being a Nagaraja) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the changes to her were particularly well thought out. It makes sense, too. I think that it highlights a weakness of VTM; it has so many bloodlines that might serve better as non-Kindred supernatural elements. It also helps to create an environment - and atmosphere - that has Kindred being part of a larger - scarier - whole. That said, it is very easy to go and say such things, when you can employ so much hindsight to the game-line.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=930039#post930039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Yeah, we have some ideas about how to go with that. I find a lot of the Hollywood stuff wonderfully horrifying; that being said, I/we loathe the sewer section, so we're considering how to capture that claustrophobic, foreboding quality without the horrible tedium.<br /> <br /> And, of course, defining what the &quot;Tzimisce&quot; are...!<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Maybe you should use a shortcut? There's one now in the UP. Also, it might be an idea if there is different tunnels, and construction in the sewers? To reflect the different ages of construction? And also, there is the urban legend of the alligator in the sewer... What if Andrei found one, and made it into a 'pet'?<br /> <br /> In addition, there was a Tremere Antitribu in the mix... what if there had been a team up of some kind? Or experiments being unleashed? In Mexico City By Night, you had a rather gruesome bloodline that was perpetually hungry, and would embrace by attaching the victim to them, and they became a fleshy cocoon of sorts. Their blood shared and mingled, and once finished, the victim was embraced, and different. They all looked like the original experiment, and thought that way, too. Not that they had any memories of a mortal life, of course. The Sabbat Tremere were killed ff before he experiment could be finished, and perfected. Hence them being perpetually hungry.<br /> <br /> In terms of Kings Way, I propose a thought. You have the victim in the snuff film being attacked. What if Andrei stopped the film, stopped the Headrunners, and then turned her into furniture? Imagine the horror if you enter the place, and you see the victim, in a fate worse than death... turned into furniture, or an ornament. And then opening their eyes, and whimpering away, begging to be killed... I'm just throwing that in, because it might be an effective idea.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=937283#post937283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, just so. We considered reading them, or having another friend re-record them, but we liked that immersion of having the real ones. The recording we cut was mostly just Grout complaining about vampires being jerks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being someone who needs to get out more, I'd have gotten hold of a static hiss sound effect, and used Audacity to go into the sound file, and cover the offending portions with static. The tape is old, it would be understandable. But that is because I get obsessive, and need to get out more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:58:17-07:00","id":985615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=950862#post950862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something that's always irked me (mildly) is that that videogame's subtitle is basically meaningless. We decided we should change that...! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah... but is it, though?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I wonder if it is a very subtle reference and meaning, and a potential clue about the overall story. You have the clans, which are major bloodlines, and you have some bloodlines in the game. All connect to one original vampire through blood. I was never satisfied with the idea of an Antediluvian being in the Sarcophagus. Why? Because <i>all</i> blood lineages were feeling the emergence of the relic! That means that you need a <i>common ancestor</i> for the whole Kindred population to be affected, regardless of Clan. Which leaves only one option...<br /> <br /> What if Caine ruled for centuries, using his trusted Ghoul as a frontpiece? The king could operate in the day, and fulfil his master's wishes. At some point something happened, and the king was buried with Caine.Hence the mummy in the coffin. In addition, if you read the ship logs, you'll find that something was eating the crew along the way, including a superstitious Turk who had been speaking of some form of legend of doom surrounding the sarcophagus. Also, it was opened up from the inside, meaning it was deliberately built to be opened up if you are inside. The had to be an internal unlocking mechanism.<br /> <br /> Considering all of that, It might be that Jack was used by Caine to get him into the world, using the link of Blood to commune with him. Someone told Professor Johannsen about the location, and it would imply Kindred involvement. From there, he used the empty stone box to cause mayhem in the city, to have the enemies of the Anarch Movement tear themselves apart, thus getting rid of them without the need for a war being fought by the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> And the Cabbie? Maybe he was a herald, of sorts, for Caine? An observer and mouthpiece for him, when needed. Someone deeply ancient. Given the Malkavian PC's reaction, could it be Malkav himself? A possibility.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All speculation from myself, but it makes you wonder why Troika had that title. Given just how much of the game has a huge attention to detail, maybe it is a subtle nuance to be understood?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trotsky's Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=963130#post963130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><i><b>Oooooh. Catty, boss. You forgot how I could do every line by heart. You know how to break poor Gary Golden's heart ...</b></i></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone else read that with Gary's voice saying the words?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=975147#post975147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I always thought that the idea of a brand new vampire emerging onto the scene and kicking the crap out of all the things you face in Bloodlines to be highly improbable. If you can do that without any training from your sire, then why the hell are the elders in charge of everything? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> From the sounds of it, the players are somewhat more experienced (and better trained) vampires than we were in Bloodlines, which makes the hack and slash approach more of a viable option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Then again, we are looking at a Fledgling that is (if blood pool is a clue,)Eighth Generation. This means there is a lot more hidden potential to tap into, if you think about it. Also, if it is meant to be over a period of months, and you are fighting and questing every night, you'll bound to improve, and toughen up. Just trying to come up with some kind of reasonable explanation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=975147#post975147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> That being said, I'm interested in seeing the Minx Xiao battle. It's like a knife fight in a cupboard, except your opponent has multiple knives and the cupboard is already cramped enough!</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, <i>that</i> would be interesting indeed. That is the biggest single challenge in the game. The last big challenge - towering in the tower - is a two part affair, so is more manageable. Add the hit points together, though, and you have a combination larger in number than the challenge mentioned. 1,200 hit points for the interesting challenger, and 1,400 points for the two part obstacle. How do I know? Because I bought the Bradygames Official Strategy Guide when it came out, and it lists all of the NPCs' stats in the back. A really useful book to have!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=984714#post984714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Flawed or not, I played through it from start to finish <i>at least 10 times</i> before I even started looking for mods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was the same, though I was looking for a patch to sort out the bugs. So, I found OP 1.2, then eventually the UP. Whilst a challenge to mod and tweak, it is such a brilliant game to customise! Hugely adds to the longevity of the game, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1493-roshenrodesh","name":"RoshenRodesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:23:10-07:00","id":985677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=985615#post985615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree. Then again, we are looking at a Fledgling that is (if blood pool is a clue,)Eighth Generation. This means there is a lot more hidden potential to tap into, if you think about it. Also, if it is meant to be over a period of months, and you are fighting and questing every night, you'll bound to improve, and toughen up. Just trying to come up with some kind of reasonable explanation.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well yeah, but in less than a year, you go from a buck neonate to singlehandedly taking down entire factions.<br /> <br /> At least in Redemption, you had a party of other vampires following you around. Bloodlines just gives you a weapon and says &quot;have at em!&quot;<br /> <br /> One of the game's biggest downsides is how you're essentially forced into a combat specialized character towards the end of the game. Being a social type only really comes into play for side quest and a Mental type is only good for a stealth approach, which is useless against boss battles. If you want to actually beat the game, you need to use violence, whether that's beating people into submission, chopping them to pieces, or ventilating them with a storm of bullets.<br /> <br /> <br /> But that's a video game, and this is a Role Play, so maybe we'll see them take a different avenue this time around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:54:36-07:00","id":985698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RoshenRodesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-\u2013-bloodlines-ap?p=985615#post985615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyone else read that with Gary's voice saying the words?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You should hear him do it in person. Positively chilling...<br /> <br /> As for Xiao and fighting, etc., part of our aesthetic has been to play up the social choices, and use violence as more of a punctuation point. This game is actually a great deal more violent than some of my previous chronicles, but it's still toned down compared to what's in VTMB. The players have more agency to diffuse things with their powers and Social Skills.<br /> <br /> And as one can see from the fight with Brother Canker, violence is costly.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> That being said, the Xiao fight is gonna be something.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requ